window.docContents[197].resolve({"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--Working-with-Numerals--Multiplication":{"contents":"\n\n\n\ndef mul (n m : Nat) : Nat :=\n  match m with\n  | zero => zero\n  | succ m' => (mul n m') + n\n\nscoped infixl:70 \" * \" => mul\n\n\nMultiplication, like any function we will prove properties about,\nalso has simplification rules.Remove sorry and prove the simplification rules for mul below.\nYou will likely find the proofs of the simplification rules for add\nto be helpful as a model.theorem mul_zero : ∀ n : Nat, n * zero = zero := by\n  sorry\n\ntheorem mul_succ : ∀ n m : Nat, n * (succ m) = (n * m) + n := by\n  sorry\n\nattribute [irreducible] mul\n\n\nProve this theorem using rewriting with the simplification rules.\n\ntheorem zero_add_one : (zero + one : Nat) = one := by\n  rewrite [one_eq_succ_zero]\n  sorry\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Basics: Functional Programming in Lean\u0009Proof by Rewriting\u0009Working with Numerals","header":"2.4.7.1. Multiplication","id":"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--Working-with-Numerals--Multiplication"}});